ContextualCompressionRetriever
Definition

ContextualCompressionRetriever retrieves relevant documents and then compresses them by removing unnecessary text, returning only the most useful information to the LLM.

Workflow
User Question
      │
      ▼
Retriever
(Vector Store / FAISS / Chroma)
      │
      ▼
Relevant Documents
      │
      ▼
Compression
(Removes unnecessary content)
      │
      ▼
Important Paragraphs
      │
      ▼
LLM
      │
      ▼
Final Answer
Why do we need it?

Suppose you have a 500-page PDF.

User asks:

"What is the refund policy?"

A normal retriever may return:

Page 150
Page 151
Page 152
Page 153

containing lots of unrelated information.

A ContextualCompressionRetriever filters those pages and returns only the paragraph discussing the refund policy.

Real-Time Example
Hospital Chatbot

Hospital policy document:

Visiting Hours
Doctors List
Parking Rules
Pharmacy
Emergency
Insurance
Refund Policy

User:

"What is the insurance policy?"

Normal Retriever

Returns:

8 pages
ContextualCompressionRetriever

Returns:

Insurance claims are accepted within 30 days.
Required documents:
• Medical Bill
• Doctor Prescription
• Patient ID

Only the relevant information is passed to the LLM.

Another Example
Travel Chatbot

Travel guide PDF (300 pages)

User asks:

"Tell me about Ooty."

Without compression:

300 pages

With ContextualCompressionRetriever:

Ooty is located in the Nilgiris district.
Famous attractions:
• Botanical Garden
• Ooty Lake
• Doddabetta Peak
Advantages
Reduces unnecessary text.
Saves tokens.
Faster responses.
Improves answer quality.
Works well with large PDFs.
Disadvantages
Slightly slower retrieval because of the compression step.
May omit useful context if the compression is too aggressive.
